# Fire Translator

> Part of [LoPAS Open Translator Core](../LoPAS-Open-Translator-Core)

Translates wildfire and terrain data into common state space.

---

## Data Sources

| Source | Data | Update |
|--------|------|--------|
| FIRMS (NASA) | Fire location, intensity, radiative power | Hours |
| USGS | Terrain slope, elevation, geology | Static / event |
| Open-Meteo | Wind speed, direction, humidity | 1h |

---

## Schema

```yaml
meta:
  translator: fire-translator
  version: 0.1.0
  timestamp:
  lag_seconds:
  coverage_gap:
  confidence:

coordinate:
  lat:
  lon:
  timestamp:

sources:
  - provider: FIRMS
    update_interval: 3600
  - provider: USGS
    update_interval: 86400
  - provider: Open-Meteo
    update_interval: 3600

observation:
  fire_count:             # active fire points in area
  fire_intensity:         # LOW | MEDIUM | HIGH | EXTREME
  fire_radiative_power:   # MW
  terrain_slope_deg:
  elevation_m:
  wind_speed_ms:
  wind_direction_deg:
  relative_humidity_pct:
  drought_index:

derived:
  spread_vector:          # direction of likely spread (degrees)
  spread_speed:           # estimated km/h
  ignition_risk:          # 0.0–1.0
  containment_difficulty: # 0.0–1.0
  populated_area_risk:    # 0.0–1.0

state:
  status:                 # SAFE | CAUTION | WARNING | CRITICAL
  spread_score:           # 0.0–1.0
  trend:                  # IMPROVING | STABLE | DEGRADING | UNKNOWN

lopas:
  SCI:    # overall system crisis
  MCI:    # coherence between fire, wind, terrain signals
  CPTI:   # phase transition — fire behavior change
  RAR:    # prediction vs actual spread

action:
  recommendation:         # MONITOR | PREPARE | EVACUATE
  confidence:
```

---

## Async Signal Logic

FIRMS updates in hours. USGS terrain is near-static.  
When FIRMS detects rapid fire expansion but wind data hasn't updated:

```yaml
lag_seconds: high
OSI: elevated
interpretation: "act on fire data, not wind assumption"
```

